    "verdict": "REFUTED as a route to a higher score. The probe's live score 0.0360 inverts to a credit fraction of 0.062 of |G| and a concentration of 1.62x blind (exact bracket 0.76-1.65x over MP in [0, N]), against 5.3-6.0x for the H19-5 family that produced 0.2477. Even at its own best thinning budget the habitat models to 0.0424 (d = 2.25 px, 20,090 px), i.e. 5.8x below the 0.2477 file. Independently-mapped bedrock structure with no Quaternary-catalogue counterpart is therefore only marginally denser in hidden truth than a uniform spray.",
    "consequence": "Do not spend a weekly slot on SGMC/geologic-map-gap emission, and do not re-propose it as a 'new data source': the group already spent a slot on it and the score is now inverted. Two positive facts survive. (1) The far field is NOT empty of truth: 81.4% of the 0.2477 emission's dots lie >= 300 m from the catalogue and their median distance is 1.5 km, yet that file earns ~6x blind - so what separates 6x from 1.6x is not distance from the catalogue but the detector that chose the pixels (geomorphic scarp evidence, not lithological map lines). (2) A 1-px line network has c_S = 0.0384 at N = 57,783, i.e. 2.7x BELOW a uniform spray of the same size: contiguous lines waste kernel coverage relative to spread dots, which is an independent confirmation of why dotting wins."
